    {
      "id": "d33ebd02-b409-5ce4-b967-8e2af7d12edb",
      "name": "Attach Prior Year",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        600,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForAllItems",
        "language": "javaScript",
        "jsCode": "const prior = {};\nfor (const p of $('Read Prior Year').all()) {\n  prior[p.json['Account']] = p.json['Prior Year Balance'];\n}\nreturn $input.all().map(it => {\n  const acct = it.json['Account'];\n  const pv = Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(prior, acct) ? prior[acct] : 'n/a';\n  return { json: { Account: it.json['Account'], Description: it.json['Description'], Amount: it.json['Amount'], 'GST Code': it.json['GST Code'], priorYearBalance: pv } };\n});"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "f5a9b923-b6d8-5f71-98f6-00edc6806d2e",
      "name": "Review Each Line",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.informationExtractor",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        840,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "text": "=Account: {{ $json.Account }}\nDescription: {{ $json.Description }}\nAmount (AUD): {{ $json.Amount }}\nGST code as entered: {{ $json['GST Code'] }}\nPrior year balance for this account: {{ $json.priorYearBalance }}",
        "schemaType": "fromJson",
        "jsonSchemaExample": "{ \"status\": \"query\", \"issue_type\": \"Division 7A\", \"query_text\": \"Payment of $18,000 to the director loan account. Is a complying Division 7A loan agreement in place, or should this be treated as a deemed dividend?\", \"confidence\": 92, \"reason\": \"Payment to director, no prior year balance\" }",
        "options": {
          "systemPromptTemplate": "You are a senior Australian accountant reviewing one line of a client's general ledger at financial year end (year ended 30 June 2025). The client is a small Australian company (Pty Ltd). For the single ledger line provided, decide whether it can be verified as-is or whether it needs a query raised with the client before the accounts and tax return are finalised.\n\nApply Australian tax and accounting treatment:\n1. Division 7A: a payment, loan or drawing to a director or shareholder (often a director loan account, frequently coded N-T) must be queried. Without a complying Division 7A loan agreement it can be treated as a deemed dividend. Always raise this as a query.\n2. GST on GST-free supplies: ASIC fees, bank interest, government charges and residential rent are GST-free. If GST has been coded on one of these, query the GST treatment.\n3. Capital vs revenue: if a Repairs and Maintenance or similar expense line includes the purchase of equipment or an asset, query whether it should be capitalised and depreciated rather than expensed.\n4. Material variance: if the amount has moved materially against the prior year with no obvious explanation (roughly a doubling or more, or a large absolute swing), query it and ask for supporting detail.\n5. Entertainment and private use: entertainment is often non-deductible and may attract FBT. Note this in your reason, but you may still verify the line unless the amount is large or clearly personal.\n\nOutput rules:\n- status must be exactly \"verified\" or \"query\".\n- Set status to \"query\" for any line matching rules 1 to 4.\n- For clean lines that tie reasonably to the prior year and carry a sensible GST code, set status \"verified\", confidence 85 or higher, issue_type empty, query_text empty.\n- query_text must be a direct question to send the client, in a professional accountant's voice, referencing the dollar amount.\n- issue_type is a short label such as \"Division 7A\", \"GST on GST-free supply\", \"Capital vs revenue\", \"Material variance\", \"Entertainment\".\n- confidence is 0 to 100.\n- reason is one short line explaining the call.\n- Wages, superannuation and PAYG are payroll items, not Division 7A items; verify them if they look normal."
        }
      }
    },
